        We earn a commission when you sign up through our link. This doesn't affect our review.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">DreamHost is the safe long-game pick. After nearly three decades in the business, they have the uptime track record and a 97-day refund policy that almost no competitor matches. For LAMP/WordPress, the Managed VPS is a clean fit. For more control, DreamCompute gives you raw OpenStack instances at AWS-like pricing without the AWS complexity — useful for AI agents and side projects that need root access without the egress fees.</p>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
